      "ios_language": "swift+rust",
      "ios_platform_delta": "iOS keeps the request boundary in MahayanaCoordinator and delegates terminal truth to the iOS-owned Rust Host. feature.execute atomically registers accepted operationId for terminal waiting; feature.awaitOperation pumps canonical Runtime events and re-enqueues renderer-visible Host events instead of creating a second event owner.",
      "implementation_status": "implemented",
      "production_evidence": "source/mahayana-agent-coordinator/MahayanaCoordinator.swift; source/packages/mahayana-rs/mahayana-app-host/src/lib.rs; source/packages/mahayana-rs/mahayana-feature-host/src/implementation.rs",
      "test_evidence": "mobile/ios/FabushiTests/LocalHostRecoveryTests.swift; source/packages/mahayana-rs/mahayana-feature-host/src/implementation.rs",
      "notes": "Rebaseline from Desktop PR #20; previous Grok-direct status is not inherited. Rebaselined for Desktop PR #20 3e735e6e: Coordinator now owns explicit awaitTurn parsing; only boolean true requests renderer request settlement at Runner terminal. Workflow-reference run-now stamps awaitTurn=true and source=workflow-reference. iOS has no equivalent terminal-wait routing owner yet; status invalidated pending production port. iOS production port now treats only literal awaitTurn=true on feature.execute as terminal-wait semantics. The same accepted operationId is held until Host-owned terminal completion/interruption/failure; cancellation cleans only the waiter registration. Exact-HEAD CI is still required before verified."
